title: "Algorithmic Resolution and Solver-Dependent Observational Geometry in SAT Solution Spaces"
authors:
  - family-names: "De Jesus"
    given-names: "Elias"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0190-9143"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
date-released: 2026-09-29
version: "0.2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/innerlightr-wq/algorithmic-resolution-sat"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A geometric framework distinguishing SAT solution-space coverage from
  geometric and connectivity fidelity, formalizing the separation between
  the intrinsic solution space S_I and an algorithm's observed subset
  A(I). Includes a corrected discrete distinguishability theorem, a
  correctly-attributed connectivity-stability bound with an independently
  verified sharpness result, a proof that coverage and resolution are
  logically independent, and held-out empirical evidence that WalkSAT and
  a CDCL solver (Glucose3) trade off oppositely on resolution and
  connectivity fidelity at matched coverage on the same solution spaces.
keywords:
  - satisfiability
  - SAT solving
  - solution space geometry
  - Hausdorff distance
  - persistent homology
  - WalkSAT
  - CDCL
  - Glucose
